roll.prompt:
Use case: identity-preserve
Asset type: complete-body animation sprite sheet for an existing realistic desktop pet.
Input image 1: identity reference only, Rousong, an adult brown mackerel tabby with warm brown dense striped fur, yellow-green eyes, pale muzzle and chin, ringed tail. Same realistic adult cat, not a baby or cartoon.
Primary request: one chronological 16-frame sequence of this cat deliberately lying down, rolling onto its back to show its belly, and returning upright. EXACTLY 4 columns by 4 rows in reading order. TRUE TRANSPARENT background, no floor, no shadows. Each cell same size, entire cat and tail completely visible with transparent safety margin on ALL sides. Cells must be separate, not touching, no contact sheet lines or labels. All cells same fixed camera, same physical cat scale, grounded on the same imaginary floor.
Motion sequence in exact row-major order:
1 seated calm three-quarter front, as reference;
2 front legs bend and chest lowers, hindquarters turn slightly to the cat's left;
3 low crouch with weight shifting onto one hip;
4 lowering shoulder toward the ground, head still raised;
5 fully lying on its side, legs relaxed and tail to side;
6 starts rotating chest toward viewer, one front paw curls up;
7 three-quarter supine roll, pale striped belly becomes visible;
8 on its back, showing fluffy pale belly, both front paws loosely curled near chest, hind legs relaxed apart naturally;
9 comfortable supine belly-up pose, head turns slightly toward viewer, four anatomically correct legs;
10 gentle playful wiggle, pelvis tips a little and one hind paw lifts slightly, shoulder still down;
11 begins rolling onto its side away from the supine pose;
12 lying on side again with front paws reaching toward ground;
13 tucks paws underneath, rotates chest downward to belly-down;
14 pushes chest up using forelegs, hindquarters settle;
15 rises into relaxed seated pose;
16 exact same calm seated posture as frame 1.
Every consecutive frame is one small physically plausible continuation. The cat must NOT simply rotate like a flat cutout: change the visible surfaces of shoulders, spine, belly, hips and paws coherently. No standing somersault, no jumping, no extra limbs, no duplicates, no human arms, no two tails, no distorted neck. Belly naturally fluffy, no exaggerated anatomy. Photorealistic fur and natural proportions. Clean neutral fur edges, no red halos. No props, collars, text, watermark. High resolution approximately 2048x2048.
